==Serbo-Croatian==

===Etymology===
There are several theories about its origin. It may be connected with Greek {{term|ἀδάμας||tr=adamas||diamond}}, or come from {{etyl|fro|sh}} {{term|alemande}}<ref>[[:w:Petar Skok|Petar Skok]], Etimologijski rječnik hrvatskoga ili srpskoga jezika, Z., 1971, v. 1, p. 28, ''alem'': ''mislim da se u alem može da sakriva grčka riječ adāmas »dijamant« ... Ali treba pomišljati i na to da se može raditi o istoj riječi alemande, koja dolazi u spomenutom starofrancuskom Pelerinage-M''</ref>. Another possibility is {{rfv-etymology}} {{etyl|ota|sh}} {{term|عالم|tr=âlem|sc=ota-Arab|lang=ota}} (Turkish {{term|alem|lang=tr}}) < {{etyl|ar|sh}} {{term|عالم|tr=ʕālam|sc=Arab|lang=ar}}.

===Noun===
{{infl|sh|noun|g=m|Cyrillic spelling|алем}}

# [[jewel]], [[gem]]
# [[world]]

